<!--
  ElementPlusSlotFallthrough.rozie — Phase 82 element-plus-slots auto-
  fallthrough probe (D-01).

  Single-file (no sibling .rozie producers). Runs on DEFAULT inherit-attrs
  / inherit-listeners flags — no opt-out anywhere on this file. That is the
  load-bearing property of this fixture: an opt-out would defeat the whole
  purpose, since the point is to prove the core's root classification now
  treats "one real element + N <slot> siblings" as single-root and auto-
  synthesizes the fallthrough spread onto that element.

  Before Phase 82, this exact source produced ROZ970 (ATTR_FALLTHROUGH_
  MULTI_ROOT) and ROZ973 (LISTENER_FALLTHROUGH_MULTI_ROOT) — the classifier
  counted the root <div> AND each <slot> invocation as separate structural
  roots. It stands in for the real-world FlowCanvas / MapLibre shape: one
  real element carrying the component's own chrome, with a handful of
  <slot> invocations (default + named) as SIBLINGS rather than children —
  some authored BEFORE the element, some AFTER, proving sibling-order
  independence (NodeType.rozie is authored slot-first; FlowCanvas.rozie
  and MapLibre.rozie are authored element-first — this fixture covers
  both).

  Exercises:
    - Element-plus-slots single-root classification, order-independent:
      a named <slot> invocation BEFORE the root element, a default and a
      named <slot> invocation AFTER it.
    - SPEC R6 class-always-merge: the root element carries both a static
      `class` and a bound `:class`, so the auto-synthesized fallthrough
      spread's class merges with both when a consumer passes its own.
    - A named slot alongside the default one, so the fixture isn't
      degenerate.
-->

<rozie name="ElementPlusSlotFallthrough">

<props>
{
  variant: { type: String, default: 'primary' },
}
</props>

<template>
<slot name="header" />
<div class="epsf-root" :class="'epsf-root--' + $props.variant">chrome</div>
<slot />
<slot name="footer" />
</template>

<style>
.epsf-root {
  display: block;
  padding: 0.5rem;
  border: 1px solid #ddd;
}
</style>

</rozie>
